From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: 2026-10-11
Subject: [PATCH jm-v9 030] panvk: v9 robustImageAccess2, conditional rendering and GPU timestamps biblioklept

Purpose: PanProbe vkd3d_reqs, robust_image_access2 (skip),
tess_cond_state and bc_perf failed on the G57.
- robustImageAccess2: v9 LD_TEX returns the same wrong OOB alpha as v10;
  the csf-v11/184 GPU alpha fix-up (bi_lower_robust_image_alpha_v10) now
  also runs for gpu_arch 9 and the feature is exposed for PAN_ARCH >= 9.
- VK_EXT_conditional_rendering on JM, GPU only: a 1-thread compute job
  (panlib_v9_cond_render) before each draw/dispatch under conditional
  rendering reads the predicate and turns that draw's jobs into NULL jobs
  when it must be skipped. Batches of a command buffer are reset before
  any is submitted so resubmits are safe. Meta save/restore of the
  cond_render state is enabled for v9.
- Timestamps: CmdWriteTimestamp2 was a stub and timestampValidBits 0. A
  WRITE_VALUE SYSTEM_TIMESTAMP job plus an availability write; the GPU
  counter only runs while the atom carries BASE_JD_REQ_PERMON (from
  malisx2). CmdCopyQueryPoolResults with WAIT now closes the batch.
deqp-vk on G57: conditional_rendering.* 352 pass, pipeline.monolithic.
timestamp.* 236 pass, robustness2 storage_image subset 840 pass, 0 fail.
Shared-code changes are PAN_ARCH >= 9 / gpu_arch == 9 gates only; v10+
behaviour is unchanged.
---

